  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38348472",
      "title": "Creating & Using a Custom Component",
      "sourceHash": "97073cf029c6011808c7c403d3f9c381bcb018817711f558413410d6b218a142",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 4.23,
          "en": "So therefore, let's now also dive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.23,
          "end": 6.51,
          "en": "into that last task here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.51,
          "end": 11.51,
          "en": "and let's create and use some reusable custom components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12,
          "end": 14.19,
          "en": "Now for that, in that app here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.19,
          "end": 17.13,
          "en": "I will start with the header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.13,
          "end": 20.07,
          "en": "The header will actually not be reused",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.07,
          "end": 22.5,
          "en": "but still, putting it into its own component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.5,
          "end": 25.26,
          "en": "is definitely something we can do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.26,
          "end": 27.27,
          "en": "For that, in that src folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.27,
          "end": 31.62,
          "en": "I'll create a new sub folder named components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.62,
          "end": 34.02,
          "en": "which is not a must do as you learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.02,
          "end": 35.64,
          "en": "but a common convention.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.64,
          "end": 39.13,
          "en": "And in there, I'll add another subfolder called header",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.99,
          "end": 41.49,
          "en": "because in that header file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.49,
          "end": 44.01,
          "en": "I'll then add a Header.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.01,
          "end": 47.22,
          "en": "which should contain the component code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.22,
          "end": 50.82,
          "en": "Now, as you learned, and as you can also see in App.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.82,
          "end": 53.403,
          "en": "a component in React is just a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.24,
          "end": 56.7,
          "en": "a standard JavaScript function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.7,
          "end": 59.49,
          "en": "which does return JSX code though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.49,
          "end": 62.07,
          "en": "and which typically is also named like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.07,
          "end": 65.04,
          "en": "starting with an uppercase character.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.04,
          "end": 69.78,
          "en": "Therefore, in Header.js, we can create a new function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.78,
          "end": 73.35,
          "en": "and we can name it header, which is a name that makes sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.35,
          "end": 75.93299999999999,
          "en": "for a component that contains the header code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.25,
          "end": 80.82,
          "en": "Then I also want to export this as a default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.82,
          "end": 83.703,
          "en": "so that we can use this component outside of this file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.35,
          "end": 89.703,
          "en": "And then we can go to App.js and cut this header code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.59,
          "end": 96.42,
          "en": "move it to Header.js and return it there, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.42,
          "end": 98.82,
          "en": "And if I press the auto formatting shortcut here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.82,
          "end": 101.46000000000001,
          "en": "on my system in Visual Studio Code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.46000000000001,
          "end": 104.43,
          "en": "this automatically gets formatted like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.43,
          "end": 106.02000000000001,
          "en": "Now, of course, I'm using an image here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.02000000000001,
          "end": 109.38,
          "en": "and therefore, since I cut this header code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.38,
          "end": 112.533,
          "en": "from the app component file and moved it to Header.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.37,
          "end": 116.31,
          "en": "I also need to move this import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.31,
          "end": 118.14,
          "en": "So we can also cut this there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.14,
          "end": 121.233,
          "en": "and move that to Header.js like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.76,
          "end": 125.97,
          "en": "So now we got that import moved over,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.97,
          "end": 129.3,
          "en": "we got the App.js file cleaned up therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.3,
          "end": 131.13,
          "en": "but of course, now the header,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.13,
          "end": 134.19,
          "en": "the header component that we're defining in Header.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 134.19,
          "end": 136.44,
          "en": "should be used in App.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 136.44,
          "end": 137.67000000000002,
          "en": "And to use it there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.67000000000002,
          "end": 140.94,
          "en": "we wanna add a new import where we import header,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 140.94,
          "end": 142.53,
          "en": "though this name here is up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.53,
          "end": 145.38,
          "en": "since it's a default we're importing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 145.38,
          "end": 147.99,
          "en": "But you should start with an uppercase character",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.99,
          "end": 149.28,
          "en": "because as you learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.28,
          "end": 151.53,
          "en": "those uppercase characters are needed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 151.53,
          "end": 154.14,
          "en": "on your own components to differentiate them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 154.14,
          "end": 156.003,
          "en": "from built-in components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 157.11,
          "end": 162.11,
          "en": "And we import the header component from ./components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 162.72,
          "end": 165.003,
          "en": "So diving into that component's folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 165.84,
          "end": 169.29,
          "en": "then there into the header folder, and then there header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 169.29,
          "end": 171.99,
          "en": "And here in this React project, as you learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 171.99,
          "end": 174.54,
          "en": "you can and should omit the file extension",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 174.54,
          "end": 176.433,
          "en": "for those JavaScript files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 177.93,
          "end": 180.9,
          "en": "With that, the component is being imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 180.9,
          "end": 184.29,
          "en": "and we can now use it here as a self-closing component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 184.29,
          "end": 187.953,
          "en": "like this in the JSX code returned by the app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 188.85,
          "end": 190.32,
          "en": "It doesn't take any props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 190.32,
          "end": 193.14,
          "en": "because it really doesn't need any props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 193.14,
          "end": 195.3,
          "en": "We could make it configurable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 195.3,
          "end": 197.76,
          "en": "but since we're not reusing it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 197.76,
          "end": 199.62,
          "en": "we're not using it anywhere else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 199.62,
          "end": 201.51,
          "en": "There really is no reason to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 201.51,
          "end": 203.43,
          "en": "And therefore, I'm not accepting any props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 203.43,
          "end": 205.5,
          "en": "I'm not passing any props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 205.5,
          "end": 209.61,
          "en": "And if I save this, it should work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 209.61,
          "end": 211.41,
          "en": "but I am getting an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 211.41,
          "end": 212.57999999999998,
          "en": "I am getting an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 212.57999999999998,
          "end": 216.15,
          "en": "that the image can't be found in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 216.15,
          "end": 218.19,
          "en": "And this makes sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 218.19,
          "end": 221.25,
          "en": "because since I moved this image import,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 221.25,
          "end": 224.25,
          "en": "I also need to check whether the path still is correct.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 224.25,
          "end": 226.11,
          "en": "And that's not the case here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 226.11,
          "end": 229.26,
          "en": "because the header component file is actually nested",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 229.26,
          "end": 232.953,
          "en": "in the components and then there in the header folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 233.94,
          "end": 237.36,
          "en": "So therefore, this import path should be adjusted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 237.36,
          "end": 239.76,
          "en": "and I should first go up one level",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 239.76,
          "end": 242.43,
          "en": "so that I'm in the components folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 242.43,
          "end": 245.79,
          "en": "and then another level with ../",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 245.79,
          "end": 248.88,
          "en": "so that I'm in the source folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 248.88,
          "end": 251.79,
          "en": "And then we can dive into the assets folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 251.79,
          "end": 253.62,
          "en": "and then there, the images folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 253.62,
          "end": 255.363,
          "en": "and then select this image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 256.44,
          "end": 260.76,
          "en": "So with this, the error now went away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 260.76,
          "end": 262.29,
          "en": "And if I reload this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 262.29,
          "end": 265.35,
          "en": "the header is still there as it was before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 265.35,
          "end": 268.773,
          "en": "but now it was outsourced into a separate component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 269.64,
          "end": 273.39300000000003,
          "en": "Next, let's work on these concept components here.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
